KZ3 patch 1162: SSE bodies (SSE2 ops under the __SSE4_1__ guard that spu__vi/spu__iv need) for spu_absdb and spu_avgb (the scalar 16-iteration loops stay under SPU_SCALAR_HELPERS).

absdb = (x -sat y) | (y -sat x) per byte, avgb = _mm_avg_epu8 ((x + y + 1) >> 1, the SPU's rounding). Byte-wise, so the lane
order inside the u128 does not matter. Results are bit-identical to the scalar loops: tools/spu/test_vekta_helpers.sh
compares both over 3M random and edge inputs (gcc and clang) and has a negative control (a mutated body must FAIL).
